# Git Safety Guidelines

## Branch Management

1. Protected Branches:
   - `main`: Production-ready code
   - Never force push to protected branches
   - Require pull request reviews

2. Branch Naming:
```
# Feature branches
feature/user-authentication
feature/JIRA-123-payment-integration

# Bug fix branches
fix/login-timeout
fix/JIRA-456-memory-leak

# Release branches
release/v1.2.0
release/2024-03-15

# Hotfix branches
hotfix/v1.2.1
hotfix/critical-security-fix
```

## Safe Commands and Practices

1. Before Pushing:
```bash
# Review changes
git diff

# Check status
git status

# Review commits
git log --oneline -n 5

# Run tests
npm test  # or appropriate test command
```

2. Safe Rebase:
```bash
# Update main first
git checkout main
git pull origin main

# Rebase feature branch
git checkout feature/branch
git rebase main

# If conflicts occur
git rebase --abort  # to safely abort
```

3. Stashing Changes:
```bash
# Stash with description
git stash push -m "WIP: feature implementation"

# List stashes
git stash list

# Apply specific stash
git stash apply stash@{0}

# Drop stash after applying
git stash drop stash@{0}
```

## Safety Measures

1. Pre-commit Hooks:
   - Run linters
   - Run tests
   - Check commit message format
   - Prevent sensitive data commits

2. Sensitive Data Protection:
```bash
# Remove sensitive file from history
git filter-branch --force --index-filter \
  "git rm --cached --ignore-unmatch path/to/sensitive-file" \
  --prune-empty --tag-name-filter cat -- --all

# Add to .gitignore
echo "sensitive-file" >> .gitignore
```

3. Recovery Procedures:
```bash
# Undo last commit (safe)
git reset --soft HEAD^

# Undo uncommitted changes
git checkout -- file.txt

# Create backup branch
git branch backup-$(date +%Y%m%d)
```

## Code Review Guidelines

1. Before Requesting Review:
   - Run all tests
   - Update documentation
   - Self-review changes
   - Check for sensitive data

2. Review Checklist:
   - Security implications
   - Performance impact
   - Breaking changes
   - Test coverage
   - Documentation updates

## Emergency Procedures

1. Reverting Changes:
```bash
# Revert last commit
git revert HEAD

# Revert specific commit
git revert abc123def

# Create emergency branch
git checkout -b hotfix/emergency-fix main
```

2. Data Recovery:
```bash
# Find lost commits
git reflog

# Recover deleted branch
git checkout -b recovered-branch commit-hash

# Recover stashed changes
git fsck --unreachable | grep commit | cut -d' ' -f3 | xargs git log
``` 